course: dictionary
lesson: 14460
title: Words for people in a community
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A parish is a small area with its own church, and a parishioner is a person who lives in that parish or belongs to its church. Parishioner is a noun, and its plural is parishioners.
explain: Read the words around it to work out the meaning. «The vicar visited each parishioner who was ill.» A vicar looks after the church and its people, so the parishioners are the people in the church community that the vicar cares for.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in simpler words. «Parishioners helped to decorate the church with flowers.» If you change it to «people from the church helped to decorate it», the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A parishioner is a person who lives in a parish or belongs to its church.
fact: A parish is a small area with its own church.
fact: The plural of parishioner is parishioners.
fact: «Parishioners» often help with church events such as a fete, flowers and a food bank.
fact: A vicar or priest visits parishioners and looks after the church community.
exercise: «The parishioners sang together at the Sunday service.» Who are the parishioners? | Shop workers in the town centre | Animals kept on a farm | Teachers at a school in another county | *People who belong to the church in the parish
exercise: «Parishioners helped to decorate the church with flowers for the harvest festival.» What did the parishioners do? | Ran the bank in the village | Drove the bus to the city | *Helped to decorate the church | Painted the school walls
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a person who belongs to a church community in «The vicar visited each parishioner in the village.» | *parishioner | village | vicar | visited
test: Ruby says a parishioner is someone who visits a church once. Is she right? | A parishioner is a building | *No, a parishioner lives in the parish or belongs to its church | Yes, that is exactly what it means | Only the vicar is a parishioner
test: What is the plural of parishioner? | *parishioners | parishioneres | parishion | parishioner's
exam: «The parishioners of St Mary's met to plan the summer fete.» What does parishioners mean here? | People who sell food at the fete | Visitors from another country | The vicar and the priest | *People who belong to the church in that parish
